In order to further verify the remarkable adsorption capacities of H-UiO-66s to adsorb large organic pollutants, the representatives of organic dyes and food additives, RhB and TA, were chosen as target adsorbates. As shown in Fig. 9, the adsorption isotherms were measured to study the adsorption capacities of UiO-66 and H-UiO-66s for RhB and TA, respectively. The trends of adsorption curves of RhB and TA over three kinds of adsorbents are similar to that of TC, the adsorption amount of both RhB and TA over UiO-66 are much lower than H-UiO-66s evidently. The measured maximum adsorption capacity of RhB by mesoporous H-UiO-66-17.3 nm is 724.64 $\mathrm{mg\cdotg^{-1}}$ , which surpasses various reported adsorbents, such as activated carbon [31], MCM-41 [32], Ag@AgBr/SBA-15 [33]. As for the adsorption of TA, the corresponsive maximum adsorption capacity of mesoporous H-UiO-66-17.3 nm is $540.54~\mathrm{mg\cdotg^{-1}}$ , and the performance exceeds most of other adsorbents like activated carbon [34], MCM-41- $\mathrm{\cdotNH}_{2}$ [35], $\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{O}_{4}$ -MWCNTs-COOH/ZIF-Eu [36] and so on. The phenomenon further confirms that H-UiO-66 with larger diameter perform remarkable adsorption ability for large organic pollutants.
