## 4. Conclusions
In conclusion, we synthesized H-UiO-66s with mesopore structures by heat reflux condition on literscale, which can efficiently adsorb large organic pollutants in aqueous solution. The two H-UiO-66s both present much better TC capture abilities compared with original UiO-66. Notably, H-UiO-66-17.3 nm exhibits the maximum adsorption capacity of $666.67~\mathrm{mg\cdotg^{-1}}$ as well as the removal efficiency of more than $99\%$ . We speculate that both the interaction force between TC and adsorbents as well as pore structures of H-UiO-66s promote the TC adsorption behavior. In addition, H-UiO-66-17.3 nm also has remarkably adsorption performance by adsorbing RhB and TA in water, the uptake capacities of well-behaved adsorbent are as high as ${724.64~\mathrm{mg{\cdotg}^{-1}}}$ for RhB and 540.54 $\mathbf{mg\cdotg^{-1}}$ for TA, outperforming various reported sorbent materials, respectively. Our work successfully prepared two H-UiO-66s on liter scale under reflux condition which were used to capture the various large organic pollutants in wastewater, and it has certain reference significance to the future adsorption research.
